Subject: Keep terminal display cells independent of the public wchar_t ABI

Base: libedit-20240808-3.1 after the pinned MSYS recipe patch.
Apply after recipe adoption; the independent read.c ioctl patch is unaffected.

MSYS has 16-bit wchar_t and 32-bit wint_t. Screen cells hold both characters
and the existing 32-bit EL_LITERAL / MB_FILL_CHAR values, not wchar_t strings.
Keep the upstream wint_t allocation and literal representation, and make all
screen diff/copy/length/output paths operate on wint_t elements without pointer
casts. Convert real wchar_t visual text element-by-element at the boundary.
Keep DEBUG_REFRESH usable without passing display cells to wchar_t codecs.
Pad before wrapping a double-column literal, as re_putc already does for text.

